WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:02.960
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.010
we wanted to find out
the biggest differences

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.670
between Subway in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.587
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.200
In Japan, our sandwiches
come in three sizes.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.770
This one is regular,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.480
and here we've got foot-long sub,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:28.070
and this one right here is party tray.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.870
This is party tray A,

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.200
which is three regular sandwiches

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.325
cut into 12 pieces,

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:36.860
or we can also get a party tray

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.280
that's three foot-long subs.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.723
In the US, you have three sizes:

00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:43.990
6-inch, foot-long, and the party tray.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.710
This is five foot-longs
cut into three sections,

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.830
giving us 15 sandwiches.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.420
Not enough party in that party platter?

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.480
Subway's got you covered.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.693
Here in the US, you can
also get a 3-foot party sub.

00:00:56.607 --> 00:00:58.950
Whoa!

00:00:58.950 --> 00:00:59.783
Yes.

00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:01.360
♪ Yes! ♪

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.810
Time to give this sandwich an exam.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.890
Dude, are you kidding me?

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.060
Look at this.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.040
I'm seeing ham. I'm seeing
turkey. I'm seeing cheese.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.906
And also we have a giant sub.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.689
Let me show you.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:17.183
[grunts]

00:01:20.155 --> 00:01:21.305
I got this.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.441
And this is what it looks like.

00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:28.469
This is too big.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.040
In Japan, our fountain
drinks come in three sizes.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.370
This one is small,

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.000
and medium,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.344
and large.

00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:48.080
Here in the US Subway, the
website says there's a small,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.180
but I talked to the Subway manager,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.140
and they assured me
they don't have a small,

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.140
so apparently our fountain
drinks are just two sizes.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.026
Medium, which makes no sense
'cause there's no small,

00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:00.284
and large.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.818
At Subway, I had to fill up, myself,

00:02:07.818 --> 00:02:09.710
the fountain drinks, which
of course I don't mind.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:13.000
So any inaccuracies rest on my shoulders

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.017
and my shoulders alone.

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:19.912
Ooh!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.760
40 what? Not even close.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.680
And that was like, I
filled this up to the brim.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.940
I'm looking through this,
and I'm seeing 33, maybe.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.910
We'll be generous. We'll give them 34.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.780
They still missed it by 6.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.030
6 fluid ounces you guys
are skimping on us?

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.302
You get a good shot of that.

00:02:36.302 --> 00:02:39.210
Is that really 6 missing ounces?

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:42.030
Do we think that's 6 ounces
of fluid we're missing there?

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.670
You better believe I'm on
a high horse right now.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.247
This is infuriating!

00:02:45.247 --> 00:02:47.160
I'm really hungry, that has
a lot to do with it too.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.160
On the surface, both countries'
sandwiches look the same,

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.730
but we wanted to get a closer look.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.180
Here we have a foot-long on
white turkey with lettuce,

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.312
tomato, black olives, and onions.

00:02:56.312 --> 00:02:57.970
All right, I have got the same one,

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.655
so I'm going to weigh this.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.260
Joe: Wow, so pretty close.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.002
Scientific accuracy is really
important in "Food Wars," so.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.850
George: Now let's open it
up and see what's inside.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.150
Joe: Huh, only a 10-gram difference,

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.613
but ours had a lot more turkey
and a lot less vegetables.

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:18.258
Hm.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.950
So, here are all the Subway menu items

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.250
you can get in Japan but not in the US.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.100
And here is everything
you can get at US Subway

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.640
you cannot get in Japan.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.420
So, let's start with new
exclusive sandwiches.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.483
So, here we've got
tandoori chicken sandwich.

00:03:42.615 --> 00:03:44.206
Mm!

00:03:44.206 --> 00:03:47.090
The chicken itself is tender.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.570
9 out of 10.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.523
Congrats.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.440
So, next one, we've got tokumori
tandoori chicken sandwich.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.600
Tokumori means extra large,

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.800
so extra-large tandoori chicken sandwich.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.000
We've got spicy egg shrimp.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.108
So, next one, we've got

00:04:06.108 --> 00:04:09.516
chōkatsu chicken and cheese sandwich.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.553
This is not good.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.910
It doesn't have any taste.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.610
Man, what the fudge?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.120
So, first thing, I have this
huge pile of sandwiches here.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.750
I'll just try and do some hits.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.850
Here is, of course, steak and cheese.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.400
Buffalo chicken.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.233
Yeah, I don't know.

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:29.760
Maybe it's 'cause they put
all the veggies on here too.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.206
They kind of just did the standard ones.

00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:33.260
I don't think this looks very good.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.980
Ooh, the Cali turkey.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.310
Looks like there's spinach on here.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.415
Oh, and bacon! Yeah, OK.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.263
Not bad.

00:04:42.263 --> 00:04:43.690
They ruined it with the cucumbers.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.430
The cold cut combo.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.430
This is, like, the sandwich, right?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.530
If we were playing "Family Feud"

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:52.770
and the category was Subway sandwiches,

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.372
I feel like the cold cut
combo would be No. 1, right?

00:04:55.372 --> 00:04:57.700
Ooh, the Baja steak, everybody!

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.210
Straight from Baja California.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.820
You know their blast, now try their steak.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.901
Everyone in the room
just groaned. [laughs]

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.301
[sighs]

00:05:08.301 --> 00:05:10.556
I have to know, how far is
that bathroom from here?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.070
They really load it with the vegetables.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:19.070
Again, why would you want all
these gross veggies on ... ?

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.828
I want the meatball, and I
want the sauce and the cheese.

00:05:20.828 --> 00:05:23.070
I don't want cucumbers.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.070
My meatball sandwich is ruined!

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.512
I'm sneaking a meatball.

00:05:29.472 --> 00:05:31.497
Mm, mm, mm, mm.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.100
Yeah, the Italian BMT.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.987
Come on, this is, like,
the most popular one.

00:05:35.987 --> 00:05:37.740
See, you got the meat there.
Nice-looking meat, right?

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.860
Nice-looking meat?

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.801
Then you lift up the meat, boo!

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:43.651
Boo!

00:05:43.651 --> 00:05:45.890
Who ruined this sandwich with vegetables?

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.500
It is the spicy Italian.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.146
Looks a lot like the BMT.

00:05:50.146 --> 00:05:51.871
But yeah, dude, in Subway's defense,

00:05:51.871 --> 00:05:53.690
these sandwiches were made,

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.640
what, three hours ago at this point?

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.090
So, here are Japan's
exclusive regular menu items.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:04.709
So let's start with this
pizza bacon Italiana.

00:06:04.709 --> 00:06:06.257
Itadakimasu!

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.598
I will rate this 7 out of 10.

00:06:11.598 --> 00:06:14.100
Molto bene!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.696
So, next one, we've got
prosciutto mascarpone.

00:06:18.696 --> 00:06:20.830
Shrimp avocado.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.755
And I love avocado.

00:06:23.755 --> 00:06:28.570
Next, we've got turkey, bacon, egg.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.795
Turkey;

00:06:29.795 --> 00:06:32.995
as you can see, bacon, right here;

00:06:32.995 --> 00:06:35.311
and egg paste.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.810
It's not that great.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:45.103
And next, we've got
chili chicken sandwich.

00:06:47.394 --> 00:06:50.858
This is terrible.

00:06:50.858 --> 00:06:53.723
Subway, how dare you?

00:06:53.723 --> 00:06:55.348
[crying]

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:59.710
OK, I'm getting full,
but let's keep going.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.084
Here we've got avocado vegetables.

00:07:04.084 --> 00:07:05.859
Mm!

00:07:05.859 --> 00:07:08.783
Next, we've got egg sandwich.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:12.540
All right, one thing I
have to mention is that

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.530
