Chips!

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.110
Get yourself the Baked Lays.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:01.430
I mean, the undisputed chip
champion in the United States

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.430
right here, baby. Nacho cheese Doritos.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.821
A favorite. A classic Lays.

00:12:05.821 --> 00:12:07.305
When you just wanna see
what potato chips were like

00:12:07.305 --> 00:12:10.040
in the '50s, get yourself
a bag of classic Lays.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.830
Oh, Miss Vickie's! Jalapeño,
and lime cracked pepper.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.489
I don't think I've had
the lime cracked pepper.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.970
These are so good.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.120
Sun Chips.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.900
I hate Sun Chips.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.330
Here's a side that you can get in the US

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:27.770
you can't get in Japan.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.840
I'm gonna go "muscle man's" applesauce.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.180
So, here is Japan's exclusive drinks.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:36.575
This one right here is iced tea,

00:12:36.575 --> 00:12:39.050
and Pepsi, melon soda,

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.500
oolong tea, which is Chinese tea,

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.460
iced coffee, soy cocoa.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:47.430
And this one right here is
vegetable and fruit juice,

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:51.730
which has 11 kinds of vegetables
and three kinds of fruits.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.100
And this one right here is Pepsi zero.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.760
And this one is mocha.

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.430
Iced café au lait.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.270
And this one right here is ginger ale.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.853
And soy latte, soy mango,

00:13:01.853 --> 00:13:03.980
mango orange, mango juice,

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.113
mocha, and milk tea, cocoa,

00:13:07.113 --> 00:13:10.746
hot black tea, and herb tea.

00:13:10.746 --> 00:13:12.070
In the US, as you noticed,

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:14.920
we have Coke and Coke
products at our Subways.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.095
So we have Coke.

00:13:16.095 --> 00:13:17.285
And they also have to-go bottles,

00:13:17.285 --> 00:13:19.701
so I went ahead and got diet Coke,

00:13:19.701 --> 00:13:22.842
Sprite, and Gatorade,

00:13:22.842 --> 00:13:23.810
the fruit punch.

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.135
All right, Sauce Talk.

00:13:25.135 --> 00:13:26.735
Sauce Talk.

00:13:26.735 --> 00:13:28.510
I couldn't get any of them on the side,

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.890
but we have exclusive sauces
here at the Subway in the US.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.810
We can get a red wine
vinegar, a yellow mustard,

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.110
a creamy sriracha, a
Buffalo sauce, of course,

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:42.110
we also have ranch, chipotle
southwest, marinara sauce,

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:46.393
sweet onion sauce, and MVP Parmesan.

00:13:46.393 --> 00:13:48.540
The most valuable Parmesan, apparently.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.450
I was surprised to learn
that the Japanese Subway

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:52.530
doesn't have cookies.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:53.850
The cookies are actually pretty good.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.870
In the US, you can get
a chocolate chip cookie,

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.280
an oatmeal raisin cookie,

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:58.790
a raspberry cheesecake cookie,

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:02.280
and a white chip macadamia nut cookie.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:06.200
All right, so let's move on
to Japan's exclusive sweets.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.253
So, let's start with this
one, chocolate brownie.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.940
We've got cheese tart,

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:16.720
and this one right here
is cream soda float.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.770
And this one right here
is cream latte float,

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.025
and coffee float.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:28.310
In Japan, our 6-inch
turkey sub on white bread

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.820
is 261 calories.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.480
And in the US, that same
turkey sub is 270 calories.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:35.370
So pretty close.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:40.340
But I did notice ours has much
less sodium, like 26% less.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:44.660
Our 6-inch tuna sub is 361 calories.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.410
And our tuna is 430,

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:49.068
so a little more, but much more fat.

00:14:49.068 --> 00:14:53.030
I have not eaten tuna
anything on purpose ever.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.840
It smells like cat food.
Don't you think it smells?

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.880
I guess most cat food is tuna, so yeah.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.470
This looks super gross, but
I have to try it, right?

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:02.237
Let's see if my distaste is misplaced.

00:15:08.352 --> 00:15:09.276
No.

00:15:09.276 --> 00:15:11.080
I hate that, man.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.670
Do you like calories?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:15.870
In Japan, our most calorific sandwich

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.610
is the pizza bacon Italiana.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.920
One 6-inch is 436 calories.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:24.830
In the US, our most calorific sandwich

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:27.010
is the chicken and bacon ranch.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.810
Just 6 inches of this
bad boy is 500 calories,

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:32.500
so a foot-long is 1,000 calories.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:35.930
In Japan, our regular
sandwich with a small drink

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.430
and small serving of potatoes,

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:43.270
the total calories for
this meal is 498 calories.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:45.310
In the US, a 6-inch turkey sandwich

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.417
with a small drink, which
the Subway I went to

00:15:47.417 --> 00:15:48.617
said they do not have,

00:15:48.617 --> 00:15:50.992
and a bag of chips, I went
with the classic Lays,

00:15:50.992 --> 00:15:53.630
is 750 calories.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:57.355
In Japan, this meal total is 790 yen,

00:15:57.355 --> 00:16:00.150
or $7.23 US.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:03.280
In the US, that same meal is $9.14,

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:07.105
or about 998.26 Japanese yen.

00:16:07.105 --> 00:16:10.410
Roughly 26.4% increase.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.500
In Japan, we focus on
having a healthy diet,

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.650
or chōkatsu meals.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.200
Chōkatsu means having a healthy diet

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.120
that contains a lot of dietary fiber

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.520
in order to keep your
intestinal environment healthy.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:28.360
And it's getting common in
Japan to have chōkatsu meals

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:31.060
at home or even at restaurants,

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:35.900
because a lot of Japanese people
have a constipation problem

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:40.150
due to a lot of stress
and lack of exercise.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.800
So Subway offers a special meal

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.910
called chōkatsu chicken
and cheese sandwich,

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.480
which contains a lot of dietary fiber.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.505
So it's going to help you return to your

00:16:50.505 --> 00:16:52.655
regular bowel movements,

00:16:52.655 --> 00:16:56.950
and you can start your day with a No. 2.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:58.600
So, we don't have anything like that,

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.530
but I can only speak for myself that

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:04.640
if you're experiencing
constipation in the United States,

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:07.507
may I recommend the steak
and cheese at Subway?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.440
The Subway in Japan does not disclose

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.100
all their raw ingredients,

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.130
but they did provide
the main raw ingredients

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:18.600
for their breads.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:22.550
Japan Subway flatbread
contains wheat flour,

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:27.210
yeast, vegetable fat and
oils, skim milk powder,

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:30.668
wheat protein, salt, sugar,

00:17:30.668 --> 00:17:33.859
barley malt powder, et cetera.

00:17:33.859 --> 00:17:35.820
Well, our Subway in the US
does gives us the ingredients,

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.230
and our flatbread contains all of this.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.450
Now, there's a few similar ingredients,

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.930
and there's a bunch that are pretty close.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.410
That "Etc." in the Japan
flatbread, that gives me pause.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.970
I mean, if that's supposed to represent

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:51.010
all of this other stuff,
that is a huge dot dot dot,

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:54.030
or to be continued, or yada yada yada,

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.520
that Japan's throwing at their customers.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:59.510
I mean, if America has
proven anything, it's like,

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.210
you can tell us what's in
the food, we don't care,

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:02.043
we'll still eat it.

00:18:02.043 --> 00:18:04.070
So, I don't know what's
up with the etc., guys.

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:06.730
Subway's tuna was a bit
controversial here in the US

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.760
starting in January,

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.560
where a class action
lawsuit made false claims

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.170
about their tuna meat.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.160
The drama continued when
a New York Times article

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.077
claiming to have had a lab

00:18:16.077 --> 00:18:18.693
analyze 60 inches' worth of Subway tuna

00:18:18.693 --> 00:18:19.643
shared the results,

00:18:19.643 --> 00:18:22.610
saying they could not
identify a species of fish

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:26.580
and, "No amplifiable tuna DNA
was present in the sample."

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:27.820
Subway responded, of course,

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.180
saying it uses 100% wild-caught tuna

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:31.726
and even launched a website,

00:18:31.726 --> 00:18:34.150
Subwaytunafacts.com,

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:36.480
to give everyone a clear
and transparent look

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.450
into their tuna process.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.500
Furthermore, USA Today did
their own fact-checking

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.110
and had its doubts about how The Times

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:45.360
tested the tuna samples and pointed out

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.310
the lab tested for five
tuna species out of 15

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.670
and concluded the tuna was too processed,

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.430
or that there was no tuna DNA.

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:55.170
Different tests have detected
tuna in Subway sandwiches,

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.542
and experts say canned tuna

00:18:56.542 --> 00:18:58.333
can become denatured when cooked.

00:18:58.333 --> 00:18:59.870
Then I did my own scientific research

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.300
to find out what denatured means,

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.437
and the scientists at Dictionary.com said,

00:19:03.437 --> 00:19:06.300
"Dear Joe, thanks for reaching
out to Dictionary.com!

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.540
The word denatured means 'to
destroy the characteristic

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.890
properties of (a protein or
biological macromolecule)

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:14.550
by heat, acidity, or
other effects that disrupt

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.020
its molecular conformation."

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.107
They went on to say,

00:19:17.107 --> 00:19:18.650
"For further definition inquiries

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:21.330
please just use the search
function on the home page

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.140
as that is what it's there
for, don't email us."

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.310
So, believe what you want.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.250
Another Subway ingredient controversy

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:29.660
that's a bit more clean-cut,

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.210
at least for the good people of Ireland,

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.110
is that an Irish court ruled Subway

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:36.990
cannot call their bread bread
due to its high sugar content.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.340
In Ireland, for bread
to be considered bread,

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.830
the amount of sugar in the dough

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.200
must be 2% the flour's weight.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.480
Subway's bread, however,
the sugar content is 9.2%.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:49.090
If you're new to "Food Wars," hello.

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:50.830
We actually have a whole nother series

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.450
where we compare the US and the UK.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:54.670
You can watch every one of
those episodes right now.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.513
Click the floating box near my head.

